Package: DORAM
Type: Package
Title: Depth-Aware Structural-Absence and Zero-Inclusive Ecological Abundance Testing
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yiqian", "Zhang", email = "zhang.16383@osu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Zihan", "Zhu", email = "zihan.zhu@yale.edu",
           role = "aut")
    )
Description: Implements taxonwise inference for a depth-aware zero-inflated
    binomial-logistic-normal model for microbiome count data. The package uses
    a restricted nuisance-projected score to test equality of the latent
    structural-absence probability (equivalently, equality of occupancy), an
    all-sample zero-inclusive read-relative ecological abundance contrast, and
    a covariance-aware two-degree-of-freedom joint null. Inference uses
    analytic empirical-sandwich chi-squared calibration without bootstrap or
    multiplier resampling, pseudocounts, zero removal, or positive-count-only
    preprocessing.
